- `raw: unknown` means nothing can be trusted at compile time, so every field is checked at runtime before use.
- The type guard `isPlainObject` narrows `raw` to `Record<string, unknown>`, making destructuring type-safe.
- `timestamp` accepts epoch milliseconds or an ISO date string and is normalized to epoch milliseconds.
- `payload` is restricted to a plain object (arrays and `null` are rejected) and typed as `Record<string, unknown>` so callers must narrow its contents themselves.

